The n-th summand of the embedding i_∞ is the Scott map from D_∞ to [D_∞ → D_∞] sending x to i_{n∞} ∘ x_{n+1} ∘ j_{∞n}, where x_{n+1} is the (n+1)-st component of x. It is the composite of the component projection onto level n+1 with conjugation by the pair (i_{n∞}, j_{∞n}). `iInfTerm.apply` says that this summand, evaluated at an element x of D_∞ and then at an element z, equals the level-n embedding applied to the (n+1)-st component of x at the level-n projection of z. The two sides are definitionally equal.
